{"name":"Blue Promise","hex":"#729cc2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"promise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oath or affirmation; a vow.","A transaction between two persons whereby the first person undertakes in the future to render some service or gift to the second person or devotes something valuable now and here to their use."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To commit to (some action or outcome), or to assure (a person) of such commitment; to make an oath or vow.","To give grounds for expectation, especially of something good."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Promise","blocks":[{"text":"A promise is a commitment by someone to do or not do something. As a noun promise means a declaration assuring that one will or will not do something. As a verb it means to commit oneself by a promise to do or give. It can also mean a capacity for good, similar to a value that is to be realized in the near future."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promise"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/500px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/1280px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/500px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American immigrants seen swearing the Oath of Allegiance in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImmigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg/500px-William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg/1280px-William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70